# `@afenda/object-storage` (mandatory when editing this package)

Canonical grammar: `packages/_scaffold/scripts/lib/scaffold-grammar.mts` (`featurePublicDoorFiles`, `featureTemplateBuckets`).

## `src/` law

```txt
src/
  index.ts, client.ts, server.ts, metadata.ts   # four export doors — all required
  blob/ | r2/ | _object-storage-integration/    # only three top-level slices
```

Each slice contains **directories only** at slice root — one folder per ARCH-1002 §8 template bucket. **`components/` is a folder, never a filename.**

Forbidden: `providers/`, `handlers/`, `auth/`, `env/`, `errors/`, `client/` as buckets; package-root `r2/` (use `src/r2/policies/`); `@afenda/db` in any `**/api/*.ts`.

## Agent workflow (same turn as edits)

1. Read `scaffold-grammar.mts` before structural changes.
2. After edits: run and **paste output** (never claim pass without it):

```bash
pnpm --filter @afenda/object-storage layout:check
pnpm --filter @afenda/object-storage typecheck
pnpm --filter @afenda/object-storage test
```

Hooks deny invalid writes and fail the turn on drift — do not ask the user to run guards.
